Linthesia - Studio Debian packaging — preliminary development candidate
====================================================================

The user-visible name is Linthesia - Studio, and the Debian package name is
linthesia-studio. The program continues to use the /usr/bin/linthesia
executable and /usr/share/linthesia/ data layout so that existing user
configurations and MIDI libraries can remain compatible. This build
therefore conflicts with the older 'linthesia' binary package.

IMPORTANT: NOT CLEARED FOR THE OFFICIAL DEBIAN ARCHIVE YET.

The original Linthesia project contains 172 MIDI compositions, all of
which are excluded from this Debian-only repacked source archive. Being part of
the original public code tree is not proof that the underlying musical works
are freely licensed or that the MIDI arrangements are redistributable.
Many are recognisable contemporary themes. Their provenance and each relevant
licence must be documented before they can be restored to a Debian package.
Users may load MIDI files from their own lawful music libraries.

Graphics/3D models, textures, original artwork and embedded fonts also need a
complete, documented copyright/DFSG audit. The MakeHuman CC0 reference is
included in assets/scenarios/blender/humano_cc0/. No copyright claims about
unverified assets have been invented for this package.

The Debian source package can be compiled and audited as a technical draft;
it MUST NOT be uploaded to mentors.debian.net or to the official archive
until the licensing findings are addressed and a maintainer/sponsor reviews
this package and its build-dependency/test policies.

Build and installation should be tested on an isolated Debian 13 system.
For video export, ffmpeg must be present. A free SF2 bank is suggested, but
the application does not bundle user-provided soundfonts.

The source package also includes the Blender material in
assets/scenarios/blender, 27 Python generator scripts and a CC0 base.obj.
The 65 runtime .l3d files were regenerated successfully from the scripts
and an isolated copy of the editable .blend resources. Two were bit-identical
and 63 different from the published snapshots. This does NOT establish exact
reproducible artwork or independently prove third-party permissions.

The binary package is split into linthesia-studio (Architecture: any) and
linthesia-studio-data (Architecture: all) because most runtime data is
architecture-independent.

DEBIAN MAINTAINER ACTION REQUIRED: replace the GitHub no-reply contact in
debian/control with a reachable public e-mail address, confirm the relevant
artwork rights, create an ITP on WNPP, and use a configured GPG signing key.
Until those tasks are completed, this is an engineering candidate, not an
approved Debian official source upload.
